  "//baseUrl": "Every `paths` target here carries a leading `./` or `../`. Without one, tsc refuses the entry with TS5090 (`Non-relative paths are not allowed when 'baseUrl' is not set`) and the specifier falls through to node_modules - which for the @types/react pins and for `next-intl` means the program silently degrades and reports FEWER errors, not more. Measured 2026-09-09 when these configs moved up a directory: 36 of this directory's 48 vanished, and the only thing that caught it was the out-of-directory refusal in scripts/typecheck-test-dirs.mjs, because the TS5090 lines are attributed to the config file rather than to any test."
